#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:80
msgid "Contribute to ROS development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:82
msgid ""
"Anyone can contribute to the development of ROS. If you are a complete "
"beginner looking for an entry point, start with a simple contribution such "
"as fixing a small issue from the `good first issues list <https://github.com/"
"search?"
"q=user%3Aament+user%3Aros2+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22&type=Issues>`__. "
"If you are a more experienced developer, consider contributing at a deeper "
"level by designing new features, reviewing code from other developers, or "
"fixing complex bugs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:89
msgid "Review a code pull request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:91
msgid ""
"Reviewing a pull request involves carefully checking proposed changes to "
"make sure they are correct, well written, and do not introduce issues. "
"Anyone can review a pull request. If you are a beginner, reviewing a pull "
"request is a great way to learn the codebase and ask questions where "
"something is unclear. If you are a more experienced developer, you can "
"contribute by identifying design, performance, or security issues and "
"ensuring overall code quality."
msgstr ""

