#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:286
msgid "Write and update documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:288
msgid ""
"Contributing to ROS documentation is a great way to learn about and improve "
"ROS. Writing and updating documentation ensures it stays aligned with the "
"code. Whenever you update the code, you should also update the documentation "
"so that it remains accurate and reliable. Anyone can help with maintaining "
"the existing documentation. If you are a beginner, you can help by fixing "
"small issues such as typos or unclear instructions. More experienced "
"contributors can improve and expand documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:297
msgid ""
"Read our documentation contribution guidelines: :doc:`Documentation "
"guidelines <Contributing/Documentation/Documentation-guidelines>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:299
msgid ""
"Browse the documentation issue list, and choose an issue to fix: `ROS "
"documentation issue tracker <https://github.com/ros2/ros2_documentation/"
"issues>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:301
msgid "Update the documentation to fix the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:303
msgid ""
