"<Contributing/Documentation/Creating-or-updating-documentation>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:308
msgid "Test and review documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:310
msgid ""
"Testing and reviewing documentation makes sure it is clear, accurate, and "
"easy to follow in practice. It involves checking that instructions work as "
"expected and reflect how the code behaves. If you are a beginner, you can "
"follow our tutorials and how-to guides and report anything that is unclear "
"or incorrect. If you are a more experienced contributor, you can validate "
"technical accuracy, identify gaps, and improve the overall structure and "
"clarity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:317
msgid ""
"Follow a tutorial, how-to guide, or other documentation. If you spot "
"something inaccurate or unclear, provide your feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:325
msgid "Provide support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:327
msgid ""
"ROS users come from a wide range of technical backgrounds and use different "
"operating systems. Some are completely new to ROS, so even those with a "
"little experience can play an important role in supporting others as they "
"get started."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:330
msgid ""
"If you notice a question on `Robotics Stack Exchange <https://"
"robotics.stackexchange.com/>`_ that relates to an issue you have "
"encountered, consider sharing what worked for you. If you aren't entirely "
"sure your answer is correct, just say so. The community is there to help, "
"and others will step in to clarify or add more detail if needed. Helping "
"others is also one of the fastest and most effective ways to improve your "
"own ROS knowledge. Even if you don't know the answer to someone's question "
"immediately, try finding a solution, and when you have one, post that as an "
"answer to the question."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing.rst:338
